    "explanation": "The first cold Overview capture still showed Loading wallet and connecting data. The original harness waited for the header height effect but did not wait for the SDK-backed header to become ready. WalletSession replaces its initial context tree after mount, and its controls can change during SDK initialization. An initialization/DOM timing race is the likely explanation; the exact original event timing was not captured. The recheck waits for the enabled SDK-backed sidebar control and records notification button readiness, dimensions, and pointer hit-testing before each click. No application code was changed to obtain the passing recheck."
